ly about  persuasion whether that be through force  money rhetoric or reason when your  representatives go to the floor their  job is to try and persuade everyone else  in the room to agree with them which  means that there is a performative  aspect to their job think to yourself  how many times you've seen the clip of a  representative on the floor saying madam  Speaker Joe beer drinker from I rioting  wrote me this letter and in this letter  he says writing to your representatives  is literally an opportunity to put your  words into their mouths the value of  this is hard to overstate it's a chance  to have a direct impact on the way that  an issue is framed the language that is  used and the lens that it is projected  through think of how many issues today  from gender and sexuality to mental  health classism race that are defined  almost entirely by the language that  people use because that language sets  the frame how many damaging policies are  in place right now because of phrases  like boys will be boys contacting your  reps letters in particular is an  opportunity to shape language now as a  matter of protocol you always want to  prioritize the local office over the  federal office and this goes for phone  calls as well as phone calls are the  single most effective channel of  communication you have  without leaving your home unlike written  communication phone calls aren't  discretionary if you're on the phone  right now  their staff needs to talk to you right  now they can't skim your phone call four  subject and tone at 9 p.m. while  watching stranger things you have their  time right now again the reality is that  you're more likely to talk to their  staff than to them personally especially  at the federal level so the strategy the  game of persuasion that you're playing  is to impact the staff enough that the  message gets passed on clearly and  actionable and we'll come back to this  later when we talk about strategy now as  someone who hates making 