ng it's a lot of  information it's a lot of time it's a  lot of energy the advice here changes  a lot based on what the issue is that  you're concerned about so you want to  find the level where you can make the  most tangible impact with the energy  that you have available a lot of times  that energy is actually going to be  better directed a lot lower at the Civic  or state level rather than federal C  even if the federal government sets the  pace for policies surrounding say  policing it's the civic leaders who  actually meet with the police officers  who live and work in your neighborhoods  who tell the police chief's what the  citizens are saying it's a lot easier to  get your city to change how it views  mental health crises and whether 911  police or EMTs to those call than it is  to change the entire nation's stance and  that flows upwards local successes  become support for state programs state  successes become the case studies for  federal policy it's a slow grinding  process yes but it is possible so  contact your representatives thank you  for watching

